+## 9. When the retention ends: the backups bucket, then its key
+
+Your decision, when the retention you agreed ends. The bucket's policy lets only the deployment's
+backup role (removed in step 7) touch its objects, so the policy goes first; then the bucket is
+emptied and removed, and only then the key is scheduled for deletion (thirty days, cancellable),
+since a key deleted first leaves every set in the bucket unreadable.
+
+```bash platform
+aws s3api delete-bucket-policy --region "$REGION" --bucket "$PREFIX{BUCKET_SUFFIX}"
+aws s3 rm --region "$REGION" "s3://$PREFIX{BUCKET_SUFFIX}" --recursive
+aws s3api delete-bucket --region "$REGION" --bucket "$PREFIX{BUCKET_SUFFIX}"
+aws kms schedule-key-deletion --region "$REGION" --key-id "alias/{cp.namespace}-backups" --pending-window-in-days 30
+aws kms delete-alias --region "$REGION" --alias-name "alias/{cp.namespace}-backups"
